{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "chain-so2-co2e-mechanism-runspec",
    "description": "The `chain-so2-co2e-mechanism` RunSpec: 27 pollutant-processes over 26 pollutants, 2,767 rows. Reproduced from the DEFAULT database: 2,767 of 2,767 cells, worst 8.201e-06, per-pollutant sums within 7.8e-07. It is the widest run in the corpus and the one whose chain reaches furthest: every rung the others use, and five calculators none of them reaches.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES.\n(1) TWO RATE ROOTS. Total Energy (91) and N2O (6) come off the age-independent `emissionrate`; THC comes off `emissionratebyage`.\n(2) THE AIR TOXICS BY FIVE KEYINGS OF ONE IDEA. Benzene, 1,3-butadiene, formaldehyde and acetaldehyde by the closed form and the live complex model; ethanol by a SEVENTH algebraic form, a step in ethanol volume (`stepwise_property_ratio`); acrolein by a bare constant; the seven benzene-family toxics 40 to 46 by `minorHAPRatio`, keyed by fuel SUBTYPE and weighted by market share; gas-phase naphthalene 185 by `pahGasRatio`, keyed by fuel TYPE. Every path appends and the chain ratio is their sum.\n(3) SO2, `SO2Calculator`: `SulfateEmissionRate` times the supply's market-weighted sulfur over its energy content, times Total Energy. The sulfur is the one AFTER the high-ethanol substitution -- E85 burns at gasoline's 7.15 ppm, not the 8.0 it ships, which the reference shows as a flat 7.15/8 on every E85 cell when the national value is read. Electricity is absent because `SulfateEmissionRate` has no fuel-type-9 row.\n(4) A CHILD OF ENERGY. MOVES chains in kilojoules and converts to Million BTU at the end; this chain carries the reported unit. SO2 was the first child of an energy pollutant ported, and it was low by exactly 1,055,055.9 until the edge carried the divisor back (`lnk_weight`, conventions 77).\n(5) CHAIN EDGES MOVES KEEPS IN CODE. `CO2AERunningStartExtendedIdleCalculator` chains CO2 off Total Energy and CO2 equivalent off CO2, methane and N2O in its Java, and `pollutantprocessassoc.chainedTo1/2` are NULL on 9001 and 9801 -- so no `runspecchainedto` carries those edges. They are a declared edge list here, unioned with `runspecchainedto` into the one relation every rung joins through.\n(6) A CHAINED SUM OF DIFFERENT POLLUTANTS. CO2 equivalent is CO2 + 28 x methane + 265 x N2O, the weights read from `Pollutant.globalWarmingPotential` and carried on the edge, not the child: the first chained combination here that is not one ratio times one parent.\n(7) A SUBTRACTION AFTER THE CHAIN. NonHAPTOG (88) is NMOG minus the fourteen species of the one national integrated species set, clamped at zero. It is four rungs from THC, one more than the chain unrolls, and a leaf, so it is computed from the finished quantities after the chain rather than as a fourth rung of it. This is the only run in the corpus whose `integratedspeciesset` is non-empty.\n\nHOW IT GOT HERE. It sat in runspecs/pending/ from 2026-09-21 to 2026-09-22 with 1,294 of 2,767 rows, every one of them right, and a measured list of what was absent. The list was wrong about one piece and right about the rest. The three half-emitted toxics were not `data`: they needed a seventh algebraic form and two more complex-model properties (PLAN.md 7.3.23). The four remaining pieces were each reproduced in pandas from the default tables before the model changed -- minorHAP and pahGas 832 of 832, SO2 104 of 104, CO2 and CO2 equivalent 250 of 250, NonHAPTOG 104 of 104 -- and each landed on its first run except SO2, whose kilojoules were the one thing a pandas reproduction against the REPORTED energy had already shown and the chain had not been asked.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "chain-so2-co2e-mechanism",
      "hc-speciation",
      "chained",
      "ragged",
      "air-toxics",
      "so2",
      "co2",
      "ghg",
      "nonhaptog",
      "calculator-edges"
    ]
  },
